## 2) Google Maps (Location)

### Client usage
- Allowed on client:
  - Rendering maps
  - Place autocomplete (if using Places)
  - Geocoding (optional, but rate-limited and key restricted)
- Use a restricted API key:
  - restrict by HTTP referrers (your domain + localhost for dev)
  - do not expose unrestricted keys

### Firestore location format (required)
- Store on workshops:
  - `location.addressText` (string)
  - `location.cityId` / `location.countryId` (string or optional text fallback)
  - `location.geo` (GeoPoint)
  - `location.placeId` (optional)

### Querying nearby workshops
- If implementing "near me":
  - Prefer a bounding-box query strategy or store city-based filters first.
  - Avoid expensive full collection scans.
  - If true geo-search is required later, consider a geo-index strategy (planned feature).

---

## 3) Google Calendar (Auto-add workshop to calendar)

### Security & OAuth
- Calendar requires OAuth; tokens must be stored securely server-side.
- Client must never store raw refresh tokens in Firestore.
- Use server routes for OAuth handshake and calendar event creation.

### Recommended server endpoints
- GET `/api/integrations/google/oauth/start`
  - Redirect user to Google consent screen
- GET `/api/integrations/google/oauth/callback`
  - Exchange code for tokens
  - Store tokens securely (server-side storage strategy)
- POST `/api/calendar/create-event`
  - Input: enrollmentId
  - Validates: enrollment belongs to auth user and is status "paid"
  - Creates calendar event and stores `calendarEventId` on enrollment

### Trigger rule (when to create events)
- Create calendar event only after enrollment is confirmed paid:
  - after MP webhook marks `enrollments.status = "paid"`
  - OR user manually clicks "Add to calendar" (but still requires paid status)
- Must be idempotent:
  - if `calendarEventId` exists, do not create duplicate events

### Event content guidelines
- Event title: workshop title
- Description: address + teacher contact + app link
- Location: addressText (and optionally map link)
- Start/end: from `sessions.startAt/endAt`

---

## Cross-integration constraints

### Never block MVP
- Integrations must be feature-flagged:
  - If MP/Calendar not implemented yet, enrollment stays "pending_payment" and UI shows "Pago en desarrollo" or similar.
  - Do not ship insecure shortcuts (no permissive rules, no client-side payment status).

### File placement conventions
- API routes:
  - `src/app/api/payments/mercadopago/*`
  - `src/app/api/integrations/google/*`
  - `src/app/api/calendar/*`
- Services:
  - `src/services/payments.service.ts` for Firestore reads (status)
  - Do not put secret-bearing HTTP calls inside services used by client components.

### Testing checklist (mandatory for each integration)
- Mercado Pago:
  - preference creation works
  - webhook updates Firestore correctly
  - duplicate webhook does not break counters/status
- Google Calendar:
  - OAuth connect flow works
  - creates event only when paid
  - repeated calls do not create duplicates
- Maps:
  - workshop location saved and rendered
  - key restrictions documented

---

## Documentation requirement
README must include:
- How to configure Mercado Pago env vars and webhooks
- How to configure Google OAuth + redirect URLs
- How to configure Google Maps key restrictions
- Which endpoints exist and how to test them locally (ngrok/tunnel for webhooks)
